## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | js/unit-tests/test_gitlabIssueLink.js | 🚨 blocking red canonical gate — 2 new tests fail on the dmtools graljs runner process is not defined reproduced on the canonical runner the same dmtools run the pack release job uses ❌ gitlabissuelink envvalue prefers the java host env and falls back to process env process is not defined ❌ gitlabissuelink nodeenv reads process env and defaults to an empty string process is not defined 145 passed 2 failed why the canonical runtime is graaljs and exposes no process global — agents md § graaljs constraints no node js apis no fs path process buffer the module itself guards correctly typeof process undefined js common gitlabissuelink js 42 but the tests reference the bare global at js unit tests test gitlabissuelink js 28 32 55 59 → referenceerror before any assertion runs this exact case was already solved in this repo for the same env ladder pattern js unit tests test sessiondelta js 976 998 wraps its process dependent suites in sdhasnodeprocess detection gh 1385 rework precisely because graljs lacks process the pr description s 10421 passed 3 failed — zero regressions is consistent with a node harness run where process exists — the node harness must be green too but it is not the canonical gate fix either 1 mirror the sdhasnodeprocess guard from test sessiondelta js 976 around the two node only tests or 2 assert through an injected env function deps env instead of the real process global — keeps the ladder coverage on both runners then re run dmtools run js unit tests run all json canonical gate — expected 0 failures from this suite |
| F2 | open | SUGGESTION | js/common/gitlabIssueLink.js | 💡 suggestion the bounded at 2 min wait is not bounded on a hung socket js common gitlabissuelink js 78 builds the probe as curl fail silent with no time budget curl has no default timeout a blackholed tcp connection blocks the probe indefinitely and cli execute command has no documented execution timeout in this repo — so the documented bound module docstring bounded 24 × 5 s ≈ 2 min cannot fire and dmtools would hang the dev leg until the pipeline s own job timeout catches it this pr introduces the first curl through bash probe of the codebase so no existing precedent covers it suggested bash curl fail silent connect timeout 5 max time 15 header private token gitlab token endpoint worst case per probe ≈ 15 s → the 2 min wait bound then holds under all network conditions evidence that cli execute command carries its own hard execution timeout would justify downgrading this to digest |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

# PR new hunks — what changed since the last review concluded

Last reviewed head: 8f457c6dffec5a188bbdadbc92841df2f8448c7b
Current head: fdb96100d489ca61216d33f33676aa010aac96c1

These hunks are the re-review scope, together with their interaction
neighborhood (direct callers/callees of changed symbols). Every line
NOT shown here is frozen: a finding on an unchanged line must show that
these hunks make the problem worse (the interaction test) — otherwise
it is advisory digest only, never a review thread.

